{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BscHJ7UjKhWRdHeubWzTyj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I have the full paper and the review context. Now I need to conduct a full DREAM review with 2 reviewers:\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n\nThen a roundtable: Step 1 independent reviews → Step 2 cross-sharing → Step 3 convergence → Step 4 synthesis.\n\nLet me dispatch both reviewers in parallel as agents, then conduct the roundtable.\n\nLet me carefully read the paper first and understand it fully before dispatching.\n\nThe paper is titled \"What Does Fine-Tuning Actually Learn? Representational Analysis of Action Structure in Vision-Language-Action Models\"\n \nThe core findings show that SigLIP's vision encoder captures action structure much more effectively than other models, the LLM component trades off local geometric precision for global structure preservation while concentrating action information into specific tokens during training, and the underlying distributed representation remains stable across different training regimes and instruction variations.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21420,"cache_read_input_tokens":22929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21420},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"18723999-1838-4cd3-86c2-800e5e9f555a","uuid":"3d9e1d11-3b6d-4e60-92b9-9e2cb1a861e2"}
